 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Anybuild

diff --git a/Anybuild b/Anybuild
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0d1c628
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Anybuild
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Generated by Anybuild v0.33.1 — https://anybuild.run
+# This file is yours to edit: add steps or override the serve below.
+
+load("//anybuild/tools:node_static.bzl", "nodestatic_build", "nodestatic_config", "nodestatic_serve")
+
+config = nodestatic_config(
+    schema = 1,
+    sws_version = "2.38.0",
+    static_dir = "website",
+    node_package_manager = "npm",
+    node_server = "node",
+    node_version = "24",
+    npm_version = "11",
+)
+
+build = nodestatic_build(config)
+
+nodestatic_serve(config, build, name = "beepbox")
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 70b4c9b..5a46bc1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -66,6 +66,19 @@ npm run build-player
 The [website/](website) folder contains index.html files to view the interfaces.
 The build process outputs JavaScript files into this folder.
 
+## Hosting your own copy
+
+After `npm run build`, the [website/](website) folder is a static site. To host
+your own copy on [Wasmer Edge](https://wasmer.io/), fork this repository and
+import your fork. Importing johnnesky/beepbox directly does not copy it into
+your GitHub account, so you could not push changes to that deployment.
+
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=johnnesky%2Fbeepbox)
+
+The [Anybuild](Anybuild) file is read only by Wasmer's builder. It runs
+`npm install` and `npm run build`, then serves the website/ folder. If the
+import page shows a different preset, select node-static (static Node build).
+
 ## Dependencies
 
 Most of the dependencies are listed in [package.json](package.json), although
